1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,814
Breathing City is a Processing artwork that connects sound intensity to a Sydney Harbour

2
00:00:05,814 --> 00:00:11,129
night scene. The bridge, opera-house shells, buildings, water and particles are drawn with
code.

3
00:00:11,129 --> 00:00:16,443
The intended interaction uses a microphone: gentle input produces a quieter city, while
stronger

4
00:00:16,443 --> 00:00:19,100
input produces brighter light and more motion.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,640
This demonstration uses labelled synthetic input in the running sketch.

6
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:30,437
It shows calm, gentle, strong and recovery states, but it is not evidence of

7
00:00:30,437 --> 00:00:34,991
a person breathing into a microphone. Mouse simulation is also available.

8
00:00:34,991 --> 00:00:38,718
The real microphone path uses the Processing Sound library.

9
00:00:38,718 --> 00:00:44,100
It responds to loudness, so speech and other sounds can also activate it.

10
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:51,053
The first code section is SignalEnvelope. AudioIn captures the selected input channel.

11
00:00:51,053 --> 00:00:57,531
Amplitude calculates the root mean square of each audio block and returns a level.

12
00:00:57,531 --> 00:01:04,010
During three seconds of calibration, the envelope collects room-noise readings and uses
their ninetieth

13
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:09,100
percentile. Staying quiet is important: sustained noise will raise this estimate.

14
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,435
The opening threshold adds an adjustable margin to the noise floor.

15
00:01:15,435 --> 00:01:19,922
A lower closing threshold creates hysteresis, reducing rapid on-off switching.

16
00:01:19,922 --> 00:01:26,203
The signal above the opening threshold is multiplied by sensitivity and limited to zero

17
00:01:26,203 --> 00:01:27,100
through one.

18
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,781
Finally, exponential smoothing uses elapsed time. Its coefficient is one minus e to the

19
00:01:34,781 --> 00:01:41,062
power of negative delta-time divided by tau. Attack takes a shorter time constant than

20
00:01:41,062 --> 00:01:45,100
release, so the city responds quickly and settles gradually.

21
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:52,916
The second section is CityScene. One smoothed energy value controls several visible
ranges.

22
00:01:52,916 --> 00:01:57,358
Colour interpolation brightens windows, bridge lights and opera-house shells.

23
00:01:57,358 --> 00:02:01,306
Wave phase accumulates speed multiplied by elapsed time.

24
00:02:01,306 --> 00:02:05,255
Stronger input increases both wave speed and amplitude.

25
00:02:05,255 --> 00:02:10,190
Integrating phase avoids a sudden position jump when speed changes.

26
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:17,100
This shared input makes the response coherent while each visual keeps its own scale.

27
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:25,286
The third section manages particles and ripples. Emission rate increases with energy, but
particle

28
00:02:25,286 --> 00:02:32,073
count never exceeds one hundred and eighty. Ripples have a separate limit of eight.

29
00:02:32,073 --> 00:02:36,436
Each object expires, and backward removal avoids skipped entries.

30
00:02:36,436 --> 00:02:43,222
Ripple strength can rise after creation, preserving the difference between gentle and
strong input

31
00:02:43,222 --> 00:02:47,100
instead of freezing strength near the trigger threshold.

32
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:53,588
The source, parameter guide, before-and-after files and test records accompany the
project.

33
00:02:53,588 --> 00:02:59,100
Hardware-specific microphone checks and real peer feedback remain separate from this
simulated demonstration.
